content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-112, AquaDyne HF-300 end-suction centrifugal pump, serial HF3-22300",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration 2.0 mm/s is below the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/B boundary, so it falls in Zone A ('New machines') of Figure 3. This is well below the Zone D stop threshold of 7.1 mm/s and needs no vibration-driven action. The report does not say whether 2.0 mm/s is the highest of the two bearing-housing readings, which is the value the manual says to classify.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C06"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing housing temperature 65 C is within the 'Normal up to 70 C' limit. It is 15 C below the 80 C alarm and 25 C below the 90 C trip. The manual limit is for housing-surface measurement, which matches how the reading was reported.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Flow is down about 20% over two weeks at unchanged valve settings, against a rated duty of 300 m3/h at 45 m. The manual gives no numeric low-flow alarm limit. The symptom matches the 'Low flow or head' row of the troubleshooting table.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "No leakage is reported, so the 'Leakage at shaft seal' symptom does not apply and the seal is not currently indicated for replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Worn impeller and/or wear rings (most likely). Performance loss developed gradually over two weeks at fixed valve settings, while vibration and bearing temperature stay normal.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Air in suction / casing not vented.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Closed or partly closed valve. Valve settings are reported unchanged, but valve position or obstruction has not been physically verified.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Check the cheapest causes first while the pump is running. Physically verify that the suction and discharge valves are actually open as indicated and not obstructed.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Vent the casing to remove any air in the suction or casing, then re-check flow. Do not run the pump dry; the seal flush is Plan 11 from pump discharge.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Take vibration readings on both bearing housings and classify the highest one against Figure 3. Record the housing temperature as a baseline before any strip-down.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If flow does not recover, isolate and drain the pump.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Remove the back pull-out assembly (68 kg) using lifting equipment. The casing and pipework stay in place.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02",
        "C01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Inspect the impeller (HF3-210, 5-vane, 330 mm) and the wear rings for wear or damage. Removal uses the impeller nut, as in procedure 5.2 step 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the seal and sleeve are disturbed, inspect sleeve HF3-455 for scoring. Replace it if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth (SB-2026-014 applies to this serial).",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the seal must be replaced, fit cartridge seal HF3-450B only, not HF3-450. It is pre-set, so no sleeve measurement is needed. Tighten the seal gland nuts to 30 Nm.",
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble with a new casing gasket HF3-120. Torque lightly oiled threads to Table 5: impeller nut M24 160 Nm, casing bolts M16 210 Nm, bearing housing bolts M12 85 Nm (if disturbed).",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the motor or bearing housing was moved, laser-align the shaft to parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Fill and vent the casing before start-up and never run dry. After restart, record flow, vibration (both housings) and housing temperature, and compare them with rated duty and the Figure 3 / temperature limits.",
      "citations": [
        "C02",
        "C09",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket. Required whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-210",
      "description": "Impeller, 5-vane, 330 mm. Have on standby; fit only if inspection shows wear or damage.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-450B",
      "description": "Cartridge mechanical seal, superseding HF3-450 for serial HF3-22000 and above. Contingency only, if the seal is disturbed or found defective.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-455",
      "description": "Shaft sleeve. Contingency only; replace if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm depth.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C13",
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "Isolate and drain the pump before opening it. The motor is 55 kW, 400 V.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The back pull-out assembly weighs 68 kg, so lifting equipment is required.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Never run the pump dry, because the seal flush is Plan 11 from discharge. Fill and vent the casing before any restart, including while venting during diagnosis.",
      "citations": [
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Stop criteria while running: stop the pump if vibration enters Zone D (above 7.1 mm/s RMS). Housing temperature alarms at 80 C and trips at 90 C.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C02"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "There is no standard time for impeller/wear-ring inspection. As the nearest reference, seal replacement (which includes back pull-out and impeller removal) is 4.0 h with 2 technicians. Two technicians are also appropriate for the 68 kg lift.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10",
        "C02"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment, if the motor or bearing housing is moved: 1.5 h, 1 technician.",
      "citations": [
        "C12",
        "C10"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part number: the manual parts list gives HF3-450 (component seal), but SB-2026-014 says do NOT fit HF3-450 on serial HF3-22000 and above and use HF3-450B instead. P-112 is serial HF3-22300, which is above HF3-22000, so the bulletin applies. The bulletin was issued 14 March 2026 and supersedes the manual for this serial range.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal gland nut torque: manual Table 5 gives 25 Nm (M10), but SB-2026-014 gives 30 Nm for HF3-450B. Use 30 Nm on this pump (serial HF3-22300). Other Table 5 torques are not changed by the bulletin.",
      "citations": [
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Sleeve handling: manual 5.2 says inspect the sleeve for scoring, without a criterion. The bulletin says no sleeve measurement is needed with pre-set HF3-450B, and to replace HF3-455 if scoring exceeds 0.1 mm. The bulletin applies to this serial.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "No part number, dimensions or clearance limits are given for the wear rings, and none appear in the parts list.",
    "There are no acceptance or wear limits for the impeller, so it is unclear when to replace HF3-210.",
    "There is no documented flow or head deviation limit or pump curve to quantify the 20% loss. Suction and discharge pressures were not reported, so NPSH and the operating point cannot be checked.",
    "It is not stated whether the 2.0 mm/s reading is the highest of the two bearing housings, or what the vibration trend is.",
    "It is unclear whether impeller removal disturbs the seal enough to require mandatory replacement with HF3-450B.",
    "There is no standard labour time for impeller and wear-ring inspection.",
    "The manual Rev D issue date is not given. The decision that the bulletin overrides it relies on the bulletin's explicit serial applicability.",
    "It is unclear whether the back pull-out moves the bearing housing relative to the motor enough to require laser alignment in this installation."
  ]
}
